IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 11 -- Offences and criminal proceedings (ss 41 to 46).
-- A penalty is a number (its size in whatever unit the Act uses); the Act's maximum and minimum are given as inputs.

§ `Part 11 -- Offences and criminal proceedings`

§§ `ss 41 and 41A -- penalties`

-- s 41: a penalty at the end of (a) a section, (b) a subsection (but not at the end of a section), (c) a section or subsection applying only to part,
-- indicates that the offence is punishable on conviction (d) if a minimum as well as a maximum is specified -- by a penalty not less than the minimum and not more than the maximum;
-- (e) in any other case -- by a penalty not more than the specified penalty.
-- src:857 | In an Act, a penalty specified at the end of—
-- src:858 | (a) a section (whether or not the section is divided into subsections); or
-- src:859 | (b) a subsection (but not at the end of a section); or
-- src:860 | (c) a section or subsection and expressed in such a way as to indicate that it applies only to part of the section or subsection;
-- src:861 | indicates that an offence mentioned in the section, subsection or part is punishable on conviction (whether or not a conviction is recorded) or, if no offence is mentioned, a contravention of the section, subsection or part constitutes an offence against the provision that is punishable on conviction (whether or not a conviction is recorded)—
-- src:862 | (d) if a minimum as well as a maximum penalty is specified—by a penalty not less than the minimum and not more than the maximum; or
-- src:863 | (e) in any other case—by a penalty not more than the specified penalty.
@ref s 41 (src:857-863)
GIVEN `the penalty is specified at the end of a section, at the end of a subsection (but not at the end of a section), or at the end of a section or subsection and applies only to part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minimum penalty specified, if a minimum as well as a maximum penalty is specified` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the maximum or specified penalty` IS A NUMBER
      `the penalty imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is punishable by the penalty imposed (s 41)` IS
    IF NOT `the penalty is specified at the end of a section, at the end of a subsection (but not at the end of a section), or at the end of a section or subsection and applies only to part of it`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the minimum penalty specified, if a minimum as well as a maximum penalty is specified`
        WHEN JUST minimum THEN JUST (`the penalty imposed` AT LEAST minimum AND `the penalty imposed` AT MOST `the maximum or specified penalty`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`the penalty imposed` AT MOST `the maximum or specified penalty`)

-- src:865 | (1) In an Act, a penalty specified for an offence, or a contravention of a provision, indicates that the offence is punishable on conviction (whether or not a conviction is recorded), or the contravention constitutes an offence against the provision that is punishable on conviction (whether or not a conviction is recorded)—
-- src:866 | (a) if a minimum as well as a maximum penalty is specified—by a penalty not less than the minimum and not more than the maximum; or
-- src:867 | (b) in any other case—by a penalty not more than the specified penalty.
@ref s 41A(1) (src:865-867)
-- src:868 | (2) This section does not apply to a penalty to which section 41 applies.
@ref s 41A(2) (src:868-868)
GIVEN `the penalty is specified for an offence, or a contravention of a provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 41 applies to the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minimum penalty specified, if a minimum as well as a maximum penalty is specified` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the maximum or specified penalty` IS A NUMBER
      `the penalty imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is punishable by the penalty imposed (s 41A)` IS
    IF (NOT `the penalty is specified for an offence, or a contravention of a provision`) OR `s 41 applies to the penalty`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the minimum penalty specified, if a minimum as well as a maximum penalty is specified`
        WHEN JUST minimum THEN JUST (`the penalty imposed` AT LEAST minimum AND `the penalty imposed` AT MOST `the maximum or specified penalty`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`the penalty imposed` AT MOST `the maximum or specified penalty`)

§§ `ss 42 and 43 -- who may prosecute, appropriation of penalties`

-- src:870 | Any person may take a proceeding for the imposition or enforcement of a penalty, or the making of a forfeiture order, under an Act.
@ref s 42 (src:870-870)
GIVEN `the proceeding is for the imposition or enforcement of a penalty, or the making of a forfeiture order, under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `any person may take the proceeding (s 42)` IS
    IF `the proceeding is for the imposition or enforcement of a penalty, or the making of a forfeiture order, under an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:876 | (3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the party prosecuting is prosecuting as an officer or employee of the State or an officer of the public service.
@ref s 43(3) (src:876-876)
GIVEN `the party prosecuting is prosecuting as an officer or employee of the State or an officer of the public service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (2) applies (s 43(3))` IS
    NOT `the party prosecuting is prosecuting as an officer or employee of the State or an officer of the public service`

-- (2): the court may order that not more than half of the amount recovered be paid to the party prosecuting.
-- src:875 | (2) The court that imposes the penalty, or makes the forfeiture order, may order that not more than half of the amount recovered be paid to the party prosecuting.
@ref s 43(2) (src:875-875)
GIVEN `the amount recovered` IS A NUMBER
      `the part the court orders to be paid to the party prosecuting` IS A NUMBER
      `the party prosecuting is prosecuting as an officer or employee of the State or an officer of the public service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order is within what subsection (2) allows (s 43(2))` IS
    IF `the party prosecuting is prosecuting as an officer or employee of the State or an officer of the public service`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE `the part the court orders to be paid to the party prosecuting` AT MOST `the amount recovered` / 2

-- (1)(b): the remaining part of the amount is paid to the consolidated fund, after the part ordered under (2) is first paid to the party (1)(a).
-- src:872 | (1) The following rules apply to an amount recovered because of the imposition of a penalty or the making of a forfeiture order—
-- src:873 | (a) any part of the amount that is ordered under subsection (2) to be paid to the party prosecuting must first be paid to the party;
-- src:874 | (b) the remaining part of the amount must then be paid to the consolidated fund.
@ref s 43(1) (src:872-874)
GIVEN `the amount recovered` IS A NUMBER
      `the part ordered under subsection (2) to be paid to the party prosecuting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the part of the amount paid to the consolidated fund (s 43(1)(b))` IS
    `the amount recovered` MINUS `the part ordered under subsection (2) to be paid to the party prosecuting`

§§ `s 44 -- Summary proceedings`

DECLARE `Type of provision about an offence` IS ONE OF
    `a provision to the effect that a proceeding for the offence is to be heard and decided summarily`
    `a provision to the effect that a proceeding for the offence is to be heard and decided by or before justices or a magistrate`
    `a provision to the effect that the offence is a summary offence or is punishable on summary conviction or summarily`
    `a provision for an offence that does not expressly or impliedly make the offence an indictable offence`
    `any other provision`

-- src:878 | (1) In an Act, a provision of the type mentioned in subsection (2) means that a proceeding for an offence, or a specified offence, against the Act is a summary proceeding under the Justices Act 1886.
@ref s 44(1) (src:878-878)
-- src:879 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to provisions of the following type—
-- src:880 | (a) a provision to the effect that a proceeding for the offence is to be heard and decided summarily;
-- src:881 | (b) a provision to the effect that a proceeding for the offence is to be heard and decided by or before justices or a magistrate;
-- src:882 | (c) a provision to the effect that the offence is a summary offence or is punishable on summary conviction or summarily;
-- src:883 | (d) a provision for an offence that does not expressly or impliedly make the offence an indictable offence.
@ref s 44(2) (src:879-883)
GIVEN type IS A `Type of provision about an offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a proceeding for the offence is a summary proceeding under the Justices Act 1886 (s 44(1) and (2))` IS
    CONSIDER type
    WHEN `any other provision` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:884 | (3) In an Act, a provision that provides that another type of proceeding is to be heard and decided summarily, or before justices or a magistrate, means that the proceeding is a summary proceeding under the Justices Act 1886.
@ref s 44(3) (src:884-884)
GIVEN `a provision provides that another type of proceeding is to be heard and decided summarily, or before justices or a magistrate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other type of proceeding is a summary proceeding under the Justices Act 1886 (s 44(3))` IS
    IF `a provision provides that another type of proceeding is to be heard and decided summarily, or before justices or a magistrate` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:885 | (4) A provision providing for the imposition of a penalty or the making of a forfeiture order, without providing how the penalty is to be recovered or the order made, is taken to mean that the penalty may be recovered, or the order made, under the Justices Act 1886.
@ref s 44(4) (src:885-885)
GIVEN `a provision provides for the imposition of a penalty or the making of a forfeiture order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision provides how the penalty is to be recovered or the order made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the penalty may be recovered, or the order made, under the Justices Act 1886 (s 44(4))` IS
    IF `a provision provides for the imposition of a penalty or the making of a forfeiture order` AND (NOT `the provision provides how the penalty is to be recovered or the order made`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 45 and 46 -- offence punishable only once, bodies corporate`

-- (1) and (2): "unless an Act otherwise expressly provides"
-- FORK once an Act otherwise expressly provides: NOTHING (s 45(1) then does not answer) || JUST FALSE for the "may not be punished more than once" limb and JUST TRUE for the "may be prosecuted and punished under any" limb
-- src:887 | (1) If an act or omission is an offence under each of 2 or more laws, the offender may be prosecuted and punished under any of the laws, but the offender may not be punished more than once for the same offence.
@ref s 45(1) (src:887-887)
-- src:888 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to a law unless an Act otherwise expressly provides.
@ref s 45(2) (src:888-888)
GIVEN `the act or omission is an offence under each of 2 or more laws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an Act otherwise expressly provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offender may be prosecuted and punished under any of the laws (s 45(1))` IS
    IF `the act or omission is an offence under each of 2 or more laws` AND (NOT `an Act otherwise expressly provides`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:887 | (1) If an act or omission is an offence under each of 2 or more laws, the offender may be prosecuted and punished under any of the laws, but the offender may not be punished more than once for the same offence.
@ref s 45(1) (src:887-887)
-- src:888 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to a law unless an Act otherwise expressly provides.
@ref s 45(2) (src:888-888)
GIVEN `the act or omission is an offence under each of 2 or more laws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an Act otherwise expressly provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offender may be punished more than once for the same offence (s 45(1))` IS
    IF `the act or omission is an offence under each of 2 or more laws` AND (NOT `an Act otherwise expressly provides`) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:889 | (3) In this section—
-- src:890 | law includes the common law.
@ref s 45(3) (src:889-890)
GIVEN `it is the common law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the common law is a law in s 45 (s 45(3), definition law)` IS
    IF `it is the common law` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body corporate`
    `anyone else`

-- src:892 | A provision of an Act relating to offences punishable on indictment or summary conviction applies to bodies corporate as well as individuals.
@ref s 46 (src:892-892)
GIVEN `it is a provision of an Act relating to offences punishable on indictment or summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision applies to the person (s 46)` IS
    IF NOT `it is a provision of an Act relating to offences punishable on indictment or summary conviction`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER person
        WHEN `anyone else` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
